<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-behavior">Behavior</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>&lt;905px:</strong> the tab bar is fixed to the bottom; tabs stack icon over label, 12px labels.</li>
    <li><strong>≥905px:</strong> the bar becomes an inline, centered 56px pill bar; the selected tab takes the tinted pill and stays inline (icon + label side by side).</li>
    <li><strong>Selection:</strong> <code>aria-current="page"</code> styles the active tab; <code>flint.js</code> moves it on click inside any <code>[data-fl-nav]</code> container — set it server-side and skip the JS if you prefer.</li>
    <li><strong>Badges:</strong> <code>fl-badge</code> rides the tab's icon (top-right); in the app bar it floats over the icon button.</li>
    <li><strong>FAB</strong> docks above the bar on mobile and moves with the content column on desktop.</li>
    <li><strong>Tabs can be links or buttons</strong> — anchors still navigate; the selection state is reflected either way.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="docs-section">
  <h2 id="d-accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The tab bar is a <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code> with <code>aria-label="Primary"</code> — not <code>role="tablist"</code>; these are navigation destinations, not view tabs.</li>
    <li>Exactly one tab carries <code>aria-current="page"</code>; don't leave it off "so nothing is selected" — screen readers use it to orient.</li>
    <li>Icon-only controls (FAB, app-bar buttons) need <code>aria-label</code>; labels and badges are visible text where they exist.</li>
    <li>Badges are <code>aria-hidden</code> with the count duplicated in the button's label ("Notifications, 3 unread") — the visible "3" alone isn't announced.</li>
    <li>Include <code>viewport-fit=cover</code> in the meta viewport so the bar respects safe-area insets.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
